From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 19:15:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Don't read unset text metrics when no font can be
 measured.

get_text_metr_size() left the caller's TEXTMETRICW untouched when the
font was selected but GetTextMetrics failed, and normalize_nonclientmetrics()
then took the caption and menu heights from stack garbage.

wine.app has no FreeType yet, so no font can be measured
(get_dialog_base_units: "base units = 0,0"). Every top-level window
came out about 32875x32778: explorer's Shell_TrayWnd, notepad, and
present_loop, whose AdjustWindowRect turned a 720-row client into
33498 rows. Cocoa clamped the windows to 8576x33 at y=16000, off
screen, and screencapture could not image them.

In that case report a height of -1, as when the font can't be
selected, and no external leading; the registry's heights then apply.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dlls/win32u/sysparams.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c b/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
index 7095e41a..f3515037 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
@@ -5481,10 +5481,12 @@ static void get_text_metr_size( HDC hdc, LOGFONTW *lf, TEXTMETRICW *metric, UINT
     TEXTMETRICW tm;
     UINT ret;
     if (!metric) metric = &tm;
+    /* what the caller reads when there is no font to measure: GetTextMetrics fails without writing */
+    metric->tmHeight = -1;
+    metric->tmExternalLeading = 0;
     hfont = NtGdiHfontCreate( lf, sizeof(*lf), 0, 0, NULL );
     if (!hfont || !(hfontsav = NtGdiSelectFont( hdc, hfont )))
     {
-        metric->tmHeight = -1;
         if (psz) *psz = 10;
         if (hfont) NtGdiDeleteObjectApp( hfont );
         return;
